 "vo_text": {
  "1": "Stop carrying a fifty pound tackle box full of junk you never use. Here's how to pack like a pro.",
  "2": "First, ditch the chaos. Never organize by brand. Organize by water column. Top tray: surface topwaters for low-light feeding. Middle: suspending jerkbaits to cover ground. Bottom: heavy jigs to anchor your setup.",
  "3": "Next, choosing the right lure comes down to one golden rule: water clarity. Murky water? Throw high-contrast brights with heavy vibration. Crystal clear? Switch to subtle, natural ghost patterns that fool line-shy fish.",
  "4": "Always match your profile size to the local forage. If the baitfish are small, downsize your presentation immediately.",
  "5": "Lightweight, tactical, and ready for anything. Hit subscribe for more insider masterclasses."
